---
title: Snickerdoodle cookies
servings: 24
cuisine: american
time: 25 minutes
source: The Best Snickerdoodle Cookie Recipe by Modern Honey, https://www.modernhoney.com/the-best-snickerdoodle-cookie-recipe
nutrition:
  calories: 181 kcal
---

Heat the oven to 350°F.

In a #large bowl{}, cream the @unsalted butter{1%cup}(softened) and @granulated sugar{1 1/2%cup} ~{4%minutes} to 5 minutes, until pale and fluffy. Scrape down the bowl, add the @eggs{2} and @vanilla extract{2%tsp}, and beat ~{1%minute} to 2 minutes more.

Stir in the @all-purpose flour{2 3/4%cup}, @cream of tartar{1 1/2%tsp}, @baking soda{1/2%tsp} and @salt{3/4%tsp} just until combined.

> Use 1 tsp cream of tartar for less tang.

In a #small bowl{}, mix @granulated sugar{1/4%cup} and @ground cinnamon{1 1/2%tbsp}.

Chill the dough ~{20%minutes} to 30 minutes if there is time. Roll into small smooth balls and roll each twice in the cinnamon sugar. Press the tops down a little for flatter cookies.

Set them on a #baking sheet{} lined with parchment and bake ~{9%minutes} to 11 minutes. Let them cool a few minutes on the sheet before moving.
